{"Grant matcher checks wrong slice - for token ID like 'onrtac:<uuid>', the grant shortcut is at characters 4 through 6 of the prefix, but the matcher checks characters 3 through 5 and returns false when the value matches": 0.9820136427879333, "When client_credentials or UMA permission grants issue an access token, their token creation paths do not set Constants.GRANT_TYPE before the encoder reads the client session context, causing tokens to be minted with 'na' grant shortcut instead of 'cc' or 'pg'": 0.5187116265296936, "Shortcut length can break decoding - encoder appends whatever OAuth2GrantTypeFactory.getShortcut() returns, but getTokenContextFromTokenId() only accepts six-character context and slices grant shortcut as exactly two characters, so custom grant factories with one or three character shortcuts will be rejected as malformed": 0.9086382389068604, "Unknown shortcut 'na' sentinel can collide with custom grant factories - if a custom grant factory returns 'na', startup overwrites that grant as unknown, and later lazy lookup can overwrite the sentinel back, making unknown-token IDs decode as the custom grant": 0.8060241937637329}